      "Language": "spa",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Spontaneous pneumomediastinum associated with subcutaneous emphysema is a rare, though life-threatening, complication of late pregnancy and labor. We report the case of a primipara who, after undergoing normal labor and delivery of a normal-weight baby, developed pneumomediastinum and extensive subcutaneous emphysema with significant symptoms within minutes of delivery. This peripartum complication is usually self-limiting when the aggravating factors are no louguer present. Management includes strict monitoring of the patient and conservative treatment of symptoms."},
